  "scope": "Modulo-five separator splitting of the twelve-site T-eigenspace groups, using the corrected row-cut trace-functional residues, the coefficient-algebra joint T,S characters, and explicit nonzero row-diagonal matrix entries of the central idempotent actions. All three T groups split in the row cut: T=1 by the nonzero residues of primaries 1 and 7, T=0 by explicit entries of idempotents 0 and 6, and T=4 by the residue of primary 3 and an explicit entry of idempotent 4. Because each idempotent action is a projection, a zero row trace residue forces its rank to be a multiple of five; combined with the witness this gives rank at least five for idempotents 0, 4, and 6. The column pairing is a trace(P e) functional, not a column rank, so no column split is certified. These T groups are unions of the joint R,T coarse blocks; R labels of the primaries are not determined here. This is not an exact dimension or rank computation and no score change is claimed."
